# Installed dependencies. Users get these back from package.json via pnpm;
# they are never committed.
node_modules/

# Build caches and coverage output.
coverage/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
.pnpm-store/

# Logs and editor/OS noise.
*.log
.DS_Store

# `npm pack` writes its tarball into the repository root. It is a build output
# for a one-off inspection or publish, never a source file.
*.tgz

# AgentTeams team state (roster, task graph, mailboxes). Per-machine coordination
# scratch, never a source file: it names this machine's members and their
# attempts, and it changes on every dispatch. Ignored rather than tracked
# because a committed copy would be a second, drifting description of work that
# already lives in the task list — and because team state must never end up
# inside the published artifacts.
.agent-teams/

# Tool state for the `impeccable` design skill. Everything in this directory is
# scratch EXCEPT the two files re-included below — the same reasoning that keeps
# `lib/` tracked (see the NOTE at the bottom).
#
# Why design.json IS tracked: `pnpm verify` holds the design docs to the DSH
# tokens, and the color values it checks live in this file (DESIGN.md records the
# light values in its frontmatter and names the sidecar for the rest). A check
# that reads an untracked local cache proves nothing on a fresh clone and stops
# working the moment the file is deleted — so the state the check depends on has
# to be in the tree.
#
# Why config.json IS tracked: it carries the SHARED detector ignores
# (`detector.ignoreValues`). Those entries are design decisions — each one says
# "this finding is deliberate, and here is why" — so they belong in review like
# any other decision. A suppression nobody can see is how a real problem gets
# buried.
#
# Both files are generated by their tools, but each carries a hand-maintained
# layer: design.json's per-entry `token` field, and config.json's ignore reasons.
# Regeneration drops them, and `pnpm verify` fails loudly rather than silently
# checking nothing.
#
# NOT tracked, deliberately: config.local.json (per-developer consent, machine
# state) and hook.cache.json (dedup cache).
.impeccable/*
!.impeccable/design.json
!.impeccable/config.json

# NOTE: lib/ is NOT ignored. It is the published artifact — the browser half
# (lib/client.js) and the host half (lib/index.js) that a `dsh plugin add`
# installs straight from this repository without running a build. It must be
# committed in the same commit as the src change that produced it; CI fails
# when the two drift apart.
